{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files /Users/sto/workspace 2>/dev/null | rg '1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling' | head -20; sed -n '325,370p' test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj; rg -n 'Zend/tests/gc_0(13|23)\\\\.phpt' test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_selection.edn; sed -n '1,160p' collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md; rg -n \\\"cljstyle|kondo\\\" bb.edn docs/agents/build-n-test.md | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/orch-lane/1793545000000-architect-p4-stress-budget-ruling.kimi-k3.1-pro.stdout.log\n  (testing \"classification\"\n    (is (= :select (:status (phpt/classify {\"FILE\" \"<?php function f(&$x){} f($a); echo count([]);\",\n                                            \"EXPECT\" \"x\"}))))\n    (is (= :p4 (:needs (phpt/classify {\"FILE\" \"<?php class A {} new A;\", \"EXPECT\" \"x\"}))))\n    (is (= :unsupported-surface\n           (:reason (phpt/classify {\"FILE\" \"<?php preg_match('/a/', 'a');\", \"EXPECT\" \"x\"}))))\n    (is (= :unknown-functions\n           (:reason (phpt/classify {\"FILE\" \"<?php mystery_fn(1);\", \"EXPECT\" \"x\"}))))\n    (is (= :no-expectation (:reason (phpt/classify {\"FILE\" \"<?php echo 1;\"})))))\n  (testing \"path predicates\"\n    (is (phpt/selected-path? \"Zend/tests/list/list_001.phpt\"))\n    (is (phpt/selected-path? \"ext/standard/tests/array/current_variation1.phpt\"))\n    (is (not (phpt/selected-path? \"ext/standard/tests/strings/sprintf_basic1.phpt\")))))\n\n\n(deftest phpt-selection-runs-test\n  (if-let [sel (read-edn-file \"test/yang/php/antlr/phpt_selection.edn\")]\n    (let [entries (remove :needs (:entries sel))\n          results (for [{:keys [id source expect expectf]} entries\n                        :let [r (engine-result source)]]\n                    (cond\n                      (:refused r) [:unsupported id]\n                      (:threw r) [:fail id]\n                      (phpt/matches-expect?\n                        (cond-> {} expect (assoc \"EXPECT\" expect) expectf (assoc \"EXPECTF\" expectf))\n                        (str (:out r)\n                             (when (:uncaught r)\n                               (str \"Fatal error: Uncaught \" (:class (:uncaught r)) \": \"\n                                    (:message (:uncaught r))))))\n                      [:pass id]\n                      :else [:fail id]))\n          by (group-by first results)]\n      (println \"php-src selection:\" (count (:entries sel)) \"entries;\"\n               \"pass\" (count (:pass by)) \"unsupported\" (count (:unsupported by))\n               \"fail\" (count (:fail by)))\n      (is (empty? (:fail by)) (pr-str (take 5 (:fail by)))))\n    (println \"php-src selection: phpt_selection.edn not generated yet (run yang.php.phpt on shiva)\")))\n\n\n(deftest gate-fix-programs-test\n  (testing \"var_dump of a self-referencing array terminates with *RECURSION*\"\n    (let [r (engine-result \"<?php $a = [1]; $a[0] = &$a; var_dump($a);\")]\n      (is (str/includes? (:out r) \"*RECURSION*\") (pr-str r))\n      (is (nil? (:uncaught r)))))\n  (testing \"comparing two cyclic arrays is a nesting Error\"\n    (is (= \"Nesting level too deep - recursive dependency?\"\n6050:  {:id \"Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt\",\n6051:   :path \"Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt\",\n6115:  {:id \"Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt\",\n6116:   :path \"Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt\",\n# P4 runaway guest investigation\n\n## Result\n\nNo unbounded guest loop was found in the e2e corpus available in this worktree. I did not add a guest step limit or alter corpus behavior: the remaining long case is a finite PHP-src stress fixture, and the PHP harness has no installed safepoint budget or host interrupt mechanism. A bound here would require a PHP safepoint integration or VM execution-budget semantics, so this is stopped for architect review per the task scope.\n\n## E2E fixture isolation\n\nRan each source through `e2e-harness/run-walker` in a daemon thread with a per-fixture timeout, covering base `programs/fixtures`, enabled P3b program fixtures (including the heap/reference cases), and enabled P4 program fixtures (including S8 generators). All completed with the 120-second ceiling; no fixture spun.\n\n- `sort-thousand` took roughly 90 seconds locally and exceeded the initial 30-second cutoff, then completed. Its source loop is bounded by `$i < 1000`.\n- `gen-c8-pending-finally-departure` exceeded an initial 10-second all-VM cutoff, then completed in isolation: AST walker, semantic, stack, and register all returned `\"E\"`. This was a timeout that was too short, not a spin.\n- The two selected PHPT sources containing literal `while (1)` also completed: `Zend/tests/bug44184.phpt` throws from the loop and is caught; `Zend/tests/bug66608.phpt` breaks from both loops.\n\nThe requested `collab/orch-lane/p4-e2e-hang-threaddump.txt` is absent in this worktree, so I could not compare the reported stack to this checkout's fixture IDs.\n\n## PHPT selection path\n\n`phpt_selection.edn` has 1,088 entries. The actual `phpt-selection-runs-test` did not finish under a 300-second wall-clock timeout. The largest selected finite loop I isolated was `Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt`: it runs `for ($i = 0; $i < 10001; $i++)`, took 258,911 ms through the walker, then reached an unsupported `gc_collect_cycles()` call. The similar `Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt` has two explicit finite bounds (9,999 and 10,001); the combined stress probe was still processing it when its 300-second wrapper expired. Other large loop cases found by source scan either have explicit numeric bounds or are marked `:needs :p4` and excluded from this selection.\n\nThese are finite stress cases, not loops that PHP itself would run forever. Reducing their iteration counts changes the GC threshold behavior under test. The harness currently runs guests directly via `run_vm` with no PHP step budget. The PHP design doc describes a future deterministic safepoint-count budget, but this worktree has no PHP safepoint hook/profile to install; shared `:line` support is also explicitly pending safepoint slice 3.\n\n## Architect decision needed\n\nPlease adjudicate the intended local quick-tier policy for the selected PHP-src GC stress cases and the mechanism for bounding guest execution. If the selected path needs an interruptible step budget, that requires the PHP safepoint contract/profile or engine execution semantics, outside this frontend fixture fix. No fixture was identified that can correctly be “bounded” at the source level without changing its meaning.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Fixture-by-fixture walker pass: completed; no timeout at the final 120-second ceiling.\n- PHPT special `while (1)` candidates: both completed.\n- `phpt-selection-runs-test`: did not complete within 300 seconds.\n- No source/test files were changed; cljstyle/kondo were therefore not applicable.\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:88:change (deps.edn bb.edn shadow-cljs.edn mise.toml .cljstyle src/dev/\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:89:antlr/ .clj-kondo/ package*/pubspec*): it runs nothing; run `bb test`,\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:290:clj -M:kondo --lint <path>\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:439:| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:440:| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:768:1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:770:   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:773:2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:782:4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
