ntinuation.md:142:9. **Preemptive migration at any pc is a primary invariant of `yin.vm`** (owner, 2026-10-17: \\\"preemptive migration, the ability to pause and continue at any PC, is a primary invariant of yin.vm. It is why yin.vm is defined as a continuation VM based on the CESK model. The UCF being only defined at a wait or parked state is a violation of this invariant\\\"). The carrier expresses the evaluator's complete task state between **any** two instructions, including the scheduler's products (remaining waits, completed wakes), not only its two delivery states; a safepoint is a boundary at which the program stops by itself. Slices 6d-a (carrier, reference lane), 6d-b (holder, custody, expiry) and 6e (backends) land it.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:640:frame from its state at a safepoint; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame` on\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1103:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` (UCF §7.4.2, as amended; the name is\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1110:`:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` rather than borrow its successor's pc.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1202:## 5. The safepoint harness\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1208:module contexts and every refusal: lift at the safepoint, lower into a\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1210:uninterrupted reference run; `lift(lower(frame)) = frame`; the frame's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1218:(`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`), whose expected results follow\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1230:the harness pins `1` for that one case (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc`,\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1268:of the old harness (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:92-106`: `:bare`,\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1313:defined and otherwise refuses it `:export-missing`. **Amended 2026-10-16 (any-pc, owner invariant 2026-10-17).** A budgeted sweep can retain a child with active control at phas