.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2045:**Budgeted scheduler round.**\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2047:Propagate the budget through `check-wait-set`, `poll-links`, `advance-installs` and `advance-install`. Each visited child is invoked once through `run-fuel child n`; nested children use the same rule. Preserve existing gate stamping and the prohibition on running children under closed gates.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2051:The dispatch tests **control presence**, not merely `engine/active-continuation?`: the latter only tests blocked/halted flags and can classify a control-less ingress-ready machine as active. Therefore no `run-fuel` path falls through `vm-hot` into its unbudgeted scheduler fallback. A quiescent control-less machine takes the budgeted no-work round and returns.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2055:Each task visited during the invocation receives at most one budgeted action and at most one bridge step. Each task executes at most `n` guest instructions. For `t` distinct tasks visited during the invocation, including children created during the round, the instruction bound is `n × t`. No task is revisited with a fresh budget inside that invocation.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2196:    [:cursor-cells]` under the default budget and 2 cells under\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2199:    `{:depth 3}` and under the default budget, and a literal nested 3000\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2205:    default budget; `{:work 1}` refuses `[:work]` at `emit` and, for a\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2207:22. Budgets: `:label-bytes` and `:search` gone, `:work` default\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2214:`test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` (§5, the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2351:    still refuses `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`, and the same pc lifts as a\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2369:    `:not-at-safepoint` refusal belongs to a pc outside every body, not\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2478:10. **Budgeted children.** Preempt long and nested initializers; lift/lower running children under receiver admission; continue to linked. Count actual instruction transitions and assert at most `n` per visited task and `n × t` overall. No child receives a second budget inside one invocation.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2480:11. **Bounded bridge execution.** A program repeatedly making bridge-served FFI calls returns from every `run-fuel` invocation. Each invocation executes at most one raw action and one bridge step. Repeated invocations reach the reference result. Diagnostic-only bridge input also returns after one step. Pin control-less ingress-ready dispatch to the budgeted round. For a pure active computation lasting at least `n` instructions, compare with `n` single-instruction steps; an earlier park/halt ends the comparison there.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2498:diagnostics); `safepoint!`'s run mode (any pc inside a body);\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2515:refusing `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; item 6 resolved by the static check\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2546:  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2697:`[sp :yin.safepoint/stack-effect -1]` with `[sp :yin.safepoint/def #{…}]\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2698:[sp :yin.safepoint/use #{…}] [sp :yin.safepoint/live #{…}]`; in the\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2703:segment to each safepoint and compares the observed deltas and E-reads.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2709:that runs the segment to each safepoint and compares the saved window's\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2726:**U6 — §7.11 (ACCEPT WITH CHANGES).** In \\\"Safepoint conformance\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.cont