`'s `:stage`)\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-504-   of a Python import under `requirement`: `{:profile name :hooks true\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:505:   :hooks-profile p :pysp address}` or `{:profile name :noninterruptible\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-506-   true}`, with `:runtime` the names of the runtime modules (default `py`,\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-507-   `pysp`) it passes through. `records` ({manifest [record-address ...]})\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-508-   are the local publication's records; a DHT source supplies none and the\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-509-   stage discovers them from the index datoms of its context. The stage\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-510-   reads only the context's `:store` and never fetches: it answers\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-511-   `{:status :missing :address a}` for the first address that store does\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-512-   not hold, and is run again once it is there. Answers\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-513-   `(fn [ctx name address])`: `{:status :ok :address address}` as published\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc:514:   when noninterruptible, else the address of the instrumented module\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-515-   derived bottom-up from the verified sets (`:derivation` its `:derive`\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-516-   record's address), or the refusal naming the profile, the set and the\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-517-   `:name` refused.\\\"\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-518-  [registry requirement records]\\n--\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-520-    (fn [ctx name address]\\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc-521-      (cond\\nResults truncated to 150 lines (total: 301). Use offset=150 to see more.\"}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_FS3fmFYjpvLALMVArCNpg8xF\",\"content\":\"test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-80-       (when uncaught\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-81-         (str \\\"PHP Fatal error:  Uncaught \\\" (:class uncaught) \\\": \\\" (:message uncaught)))))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-82-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-83-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:84:(defn run-vms\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-85-  \\\"`{vm-key rendered}` of `ast` on the four VMs; a host throw is\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-86-   `[:thrown message]`.\\\"\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-87-  [registry ast]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-88-  (let [opts (assoc base-opts :modules registry)\\n--\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-109-(defn run-php\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-110-  \\\"`{vm-key rendered}` for `source`, or `{:diagnostics d}`.\\\"\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-111-  [source]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-112-  (let [{:keys [ast diagnostics]} (lower-program source)]\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:113:    (if diagnostics {:diagnostics diagnostics} (run-vms (host-registry) ast))))\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-114-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-115-\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-116-(defn run-walker\\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj-117-  \\\"The ast-walker's rendering of `source` alone (fast iteration).\\\"\"}\n{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"tool_TGaek3O949ldhF2yefPAwUsL\",\"content\":\"No matches found\"}\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"## Ruling: both, sequenced\\n\\n**(b) Re-tier immediately.** Keep ordinary PHPT cases in the quick tier, but move the curated PHPT stress cases—at minimum `gc_013`, `gc_023`, and their e2e-derived counterparts—behind `^:slow` / `DATOM_SLOW_TESTS`. Do not reduce iteration counts or otherwise alter fixture semantics. The current combined quick test is at `test/yang/php/antlr/e2e_test.clj:340`.\\n\\n**(a) Add the budget as a separate P7-a robustness change, not as a prerequisite for lane stability.**\\n\\nSmallest contract:\\n\\n- Add an **optional, per-run safepoint-count budget** to the PHP execution profile. `run-vm` may pass the option, but must not implement a host wall-clock timeout as guest semantics.\\n- Count the existing PHP `:loop` and `:call` safepoint hooks; do not introduce generic VM-instruction accounting for this feature.\\n- Default is **unlimited/off**, so production behavior is unchanged unless a composition explicitly supplies a budget.\\n- Exhaustion is the documented **PHP operational fatal**, using the pinned PHP text—not the JavaScript `Interrupt` exception. It is not guest-catchable and skips destructor shutdown, consistent with `docs/design/yang.php.md:1239` and `docs/design/yang.php.md:1927`.\\n- This bounds guest execution between hooks; it is not a wall-clock guarantee around blocking host operations.\\n\\nThis follows the existing PHP contract: deterministic safepoint budget rather than nondeterministic `max_execution_time` (`docs/design/yang.php.md:1921-1938`, `docs/design/yang.php.md:2093-2097`). Generic engine step budgets remain an engine responsibility (`docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md:565-568`); safepoints are program stopping boundaries, not a license to change default execution semantics (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:655-659`).\\n\\n**Disposition of the 93-minute shiva sighting:** close the suspected **guest-nontermination defect now** as finite stress cost, supported by the fixture walk and measured `gc_013` completion (`collab/1793540000000-engineer-p4-hang.gpt-6-luna.findings.md:9-21`). Keep the **quick-tier lane-stability task** open until re-tiering lands; do not hold the hang investigation open for the budget work.\"}\n{\"role\":\"meta\",\"type\":\"session.resume_hint\",\"session_id\":\"session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05\",\"command\":\"kimi -r session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05\",\"content\":\"To resume this session: kimi -r session_4ebef743-ae5c-42d7-b768-c4f4f66a4a05\"}\n  and checks each section 9 failure as data. Ports are ephemeral, and\n  every wait is bounded. A run takes a few minutes. Run it alone with\n  `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl.dht-process-test`, after\n  `bb build:yin-repl-node`.\n- `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` (all three lanes): the same\n  scenario in process, over the `dao.jing.dht` test mesh seam. Dart's\n  signed-name leg runs here, because no Dart `yin.repl.main` process\n  exists to spawn. `build/yin-repl-peer` is the R5 slice peer, not a\n  REPL.\n\n```sh\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\nThe Dart `bb` lanes run `src/dev/cljd_agg.clj` (`bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\n[--slow-only | --slow-regex]`), not `cljd test`. `--slow-only` runs only the\nnamespaces that use `dao.test-slow/guard` and fails if one has no generated\nDart file. `--slow-regex` prints those namespaces as an anchored alternation\nwith its dots already escaped for an EDN string (bb.edn feeds it to shadow-cljs\n`--config-merge` for `test:slow:cljs`); it is not a ready-to-use regex, and it\nexits 1 when no namespace uses the guard. `flutter test` spends about 7.5 s loading\neach of the ~166 generated `test/cljd-out/**/*_test.dart` files, so the\nscript compiles every test namespace via `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile\n<namespaces>`, writes up to min(8, cores) shard files under `build/cljd-agg/`\n(greedy by file size; each imports its files and calls their `main`), runs\n`flutter test --concurrency N` on the shards, and deletes them. Shards never sit\nunder `test/`, so plain `clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd test` still works. Tests of\ndifferent namespaces share an isolate per shard. Failures stay attributable:\npackage:test names are ns-qualified (`dao.foo-test/bar-test`).\n\n`flutter test`/`cljd test` globs everything under `test/cljd-out/`, and the\ncompile does not prune it when a source file is deleted or renamed. The\n6048-   :title \"GC 012: collection of many loops at once\",\n6049-   :expect \"int(0)\\nint(1000)\\nok\"}\n6050:  {:id \"Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt\",\n6051:   :path \"Zend/tests/gc_013.phpt\",\n6052-   :source\n6053-   \"<?php\\n$a = array();\\nfor ($i = 0; $i < 10001; $i++) {\\n    $a[$i] =& $a;\\n}\\n$a[] = \\\"xxx\\\";\\nunset($a);\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles() > 0);\\necho \\\"ok\\\\n\\\";\\n?>\",\n6054-   :title \"GC 013: Too many cycles in one array\",\n6055-   :expect \"bool(true)\\nok\"}\n6056-  {:id \"Zend/tests/gc_014.phpt\",\n6057-   :path \"Zend/tests/gc_014.phpt\",\n6058-   :source\n6059-   \"<?php\\n$a = new stdClass();\\nfor ($i = 0; $i < 10001; $i++) {\\n    $b =& $a;\\n    $a->{\\\"a\\\".$i} = $a;\\n}\\nunset($b);\\n$a->b = \\\"xxx\\\";\\nunset($a);\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles() > 0);\\necho \\\"ok\\\\n\\\";\\n?>\",\n6060-   :title \"GC 014: Too many cycles in one object\",\n6061-   :expect \"bool(true)\\nok\",\n--\n6113-   :title \"GC 022: GC detach reference in executor's PZVAL_UNLOCK()\",\n6114-   :expect \"int(1)\\nok\"}\n6115:  {:id \"Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt\",\n6116:   :path \"Zend/tests/gc_023.phpt\",\n6117-   :source\n6118-   \"<?php\\n$a=array();\\nfor ($i=0; $i < 9999; $i++) {\\n    $a[$i] = array(array());\\n    $a[$i][0] = & $a[$i];\\n}\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles());\\nunset($a);\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles());\\n$a=array();\\nfor ($i=0; $i < 10001; $i++) {\\n    $a[$i] = array(array());\\n    $a[$i][0] = & $a[$i];\\n}\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles());\\nunset($a); // 10000 zvals collected automatic\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles());\\necho \\\"ok\\\\n\\\";\\n?>\",\n6119-   :title \"GC 023: Root buffer overflow (automatic collection)\",\n6120-   :expect \"int(0)\\nint(9999)\\nint(0)\\nint(1)\\nok\"}\n6121-  {:id \"Zend/tests/gc_024.phpt\",\n6122-   :path \"Zend/tests/gc_024.phpt\",\n6123-   :source\n6124-   \"<?php\\n$a = new ArrayObject();\\n$a[0] = $a;\\nunset($a);\\nvar_dump(gc_collect_cycles());\\necho \\\"ok\\\\n\\\";\\n?>\",\n6125-   :title \"GC 024: GC and objects with non-standard handlers\",\n6126-   :expect \"int(2)\\nok\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
